.TH "oudterminallutetablatureeditorandviewer" "1" "2026\-09\-27"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
\fB\fRoud\fB\fR \- terminal editor and viewer for lute tablature
.PP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fB\fRoud\fB\fR [\fBFILE\fR]
.PP
\fB\fRoud\fB\fR \fB\fRtui\fB\fR [\fB\-\-readonly\fR] [\fBFILE\fR]
.PP
\fB\fRoud\fB\fR \fB\fRascii\fB\fR \fBINPUT\fR [\fB\-o\fR \fBOUTPUT\fR] [\fB\-\-bars\fR \fBN|START:END\fR] [\fB\-f\fR]
.PP
\fB\fRoud\fB\fR \fB\fRconvert\fB\fR \fBINPUT\fR \fBOUTPUT\fR [\fB\-\-input\-format\fR \fBFORMAT\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR \fBFORMAT\fR] [\fB\-f\fR]
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fB\fRoud\fB\fR is a curses editor and viewer for Renaissance lute tablature.\& It reads
TAB, FT3, and supported MusicXML/MXL files, provides a compact terminal proof,
and exports TAB, ASCII, MIDI, LilyPond, PDF, MusicXML, and MXL.\&
.PP
FT3 is import\-only.\& A tab\-only FT3 opens as an editable projection and writes
to a separate TAB file.\& Scores with vocal, notation, or duet material open in
read\-only viewer mode so unsupported layers cannot disappear on save.\&
.PP
Text conversion can read from or write to \fB\fR\-\fB\fR.\& MIDI, MXL, and PDF conversion
require filesystem paths.\& PDF conversion retains the generated LilyPond source
when LilyPond is unavailable or fails.\&
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fB\fR\-\-config\fB\fR \fBPATH\fR
.PP
: Read settings from \fBPATH\fR.\& The default is \fB\fRconfig.\&toml\fB\fR, resolved as
described under \fBFILES\fR.\&
.PP
\fB\fR\-\-readonly\fB\fR
.PP
: Open the TUI in read\-only viewer mode.\&
.PP
\fB\fR\-\-version\fB\fR
.PP
: Print the installed version and exit.\&
.PP
\fB\fR\-h\fB\fR, \fB\fR\-\-help\fB\fR
.PP
: Print command help and exit.\&
.PP
The \fB\fRtui\fB\fR subcommand opens the interactive editor.\& \fB\fRascii\fB\fR renders a text
snapshot; \fBINPUT\fR must be a path.\& \fB\fRconvert\fB\fR selects the output format from
the output suffix unless \fB\fR\-\-format\fB\fR is supplied.\& When either stream endpoint
is \fB\fR\-\fB\fR, specify the other format explicitly with \fB\fR\-\-input\-format\fB\fR or
\fB\fR\-\-format\fB\fR as required.\&
.PP
\fB\fR\-f\fB\fR, \fB\fR\-\-force\fB\fR
.PP
: Permit replacement of an existing non\-interactive output file.\&
.PP
.SH INTERACTIVE COMMANDS
.PP
The TUI uses Vim\-like normal, insert, and command modes.\& \fB\fRh/j/k/l\fB\fR or the
arrow keys move; \fB\fRi\fB\fR enters insert mode; \fB\fREsc\fB\fR returns to normal mode; and
\fB\fRCtrl\-C\fB\fR quits like \fB\fRq\fB\fR: with unsaved changes it asks once and quits on the
second press.\& It also cancels prompts and closes pages.\& In insert mode letters
and digits are frets and \fB\fRz\fB\fR enters a rest.\&
.PP
\fB\fR:w\fB\fR [\fBPATH\fR]
.PP
: Write TAB.\& A first write opens a command prompt prefilled with a sibling or
default TAB destination.\&
.PP
\fB\fR:e\fB\fR \fBPATH\fR
.PP
: Open a score.\&
.PP
\fB\fR:midi\fB\fR [\fBPATH\fR]
.PP
: Export MIDI.\&
.PP
\fB\fR:play\fB\fR [\fBBAR\fR]
.PP
: Play from a one\-based bar number.\&
.PP
\fB\fR:lilypond\fB\fR [\fBPATH\fR]
.PP
: Export LilyPond source.\&
.PP
\fB\fR:pdf\fB\fR [\fBPATH\fR]
.PP
: Export LilyPond and compile a PDF.\& The default build path is
\fB\fRbuild/lilypond/\fB\fR.\&
.PP
\fB\fR:set\fB\fR \fBOPTION\fR=\fBVALUE\fR
.PP
: Change editor, playback, completion, layout, or publication settings.\& The
\fB\fRlilypond\fB\fR setting selects the executable; \fB\fRcompletion=fzf\fB\fR enables optional
fuzzy path ranking; \fB\fRplaybackscroll=off\fB\fR disables score following.\&
.PP
\fB\fR:q\fB\fR or \fB\fR:q!\&\fB\fR
.PP
: Quit, subject to the modified\-document confirmation for \fB\fR:q\fB\fR.\&
.PP
.SH FILES
.PP
\fB\fRconfig.\&toml\fB\fR
.PP
: Settings file.\& A relative name is read from the current directory only when
that file already has a \fB\fR[settings]\fB\fR table; otherwise it lives in
\fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/oud/\fR (default \fB\(ti/.\&config/oud/\fR).\& \fB\fR:set\fB\fR writes only the
preference keys it changed.\& Document properties (style, strings, tuning, time,
key, tempo, bassstrings) apply to the open score only.\& A config file containing
other tables is never rewritten.\&
.PP
\fB\fRbuild/lilypond/\fB\fR
.PP
: Default location for interactive LilyPond/PDF build products.\& This directory
is not created until a PDF build is requested.\&
.PP
\fB\fR\(ti/.\&local/share/man/man1/oud.\&1\fB\fR
.PP
: Default user\-local installation target for the manual page.\&
.PP
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.PP
\fB\fRTERM\fB\fR
.PP
: Selects terminal capabilities used by curses.\&
.PP
\fB\fRPATH\fB\fR
.PP
: Used to locate the configured LilyPond executable, and optional \fB\fRfzf\fB\fR,
\fB\fRfluidsynth\fB\fR, and \fB\fRtimidity\fB\fR playback programs.\&
.PP
\fB\fRXDG_CONFIG_HOME\fB\fR
.PP
: Base directory for the user settings file; defaults to \fB\(ti/.\&config\fR.\&
.PP
\fB\fRESCDELAY\fB\fR
.PP
: Milliseconds curses waits to distinguish \fB\fREsc\fB\fR from escape sequences.\& Oud
uses 25 ms unless this variable is set.\&
.PP
.SH EXIT STATUS
.PP
0
.PP
: Success.\&
.PP
2
.PP
: Invalid command\-line arguments or bar range.\&
.PP
3
.PP
: Input could not be loaded or rendered.\&
.PP
4
.PP
: Output could not be written or compiled.\&
.PP
130
.PP
: A non\-interactive command was interrupted with \fB\fRCtrl\-C\fB\fR.\&
.PP
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.PP
Errors are written to standard error for non\-interactive commands.\& TUI import,
playback, and export failures are shown in the status line.\& Missing or invalid
source files produce a visible import warning and do not create fabricated
score content.\&
.PP
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Open a score:
.PP
.RS 4
oud score.\&tab
.PP
.RE
Render selected bars as text:
.PP
.RS 4
oud ascii score.\&ft3 \-\-bars 1:8
.PP
.RE
Convert a score to LilyPond:
.PP
.RS 4
oud convert score.\&ft3 score.\&ly
.PP
.RE
Build a PDF and retain generated files under \fB\fRbuild/\fB\fR:
.PP
.RS 4
oud convert score.\&ft3 build/lilypond/score.\&pdf \-f
.PP
.RE
Install the manual page for the current user:
.PP
.RS 4
scripts/install_man.\&sh
.PP
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
